1
00:00:09,421 --> 00:00:12,647
Autism stems from differences in biology that have an influence

2
00:00:12,647 --> 00:00:13,433
on brain development.

3
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:17,414
Autism is a lifelong condition. That doesn't mean that children

4
00:00:17,526 --> 00:00:20,816
can't make significant improvements in their language and social abilities

5
00:00:20,816 --> 00:00:23,753
over time. They can, just like all children. But children

6
00:00:23,866 --> 00:00:25,294
don't just grow out of autism.

7
00:00:30,596 --> 00:00:33,987
Autism can affect a person's ability to understand subtle emotional

8
00:00:33,987 --> 00:00:36,509
cues, such as tone of language or body language. But

9
00:00:36,558 --> 00:00:39,801
when emotions are communicated more directly, there's a wealth of

10
00:00:39,801 --> 00:00:42,331
evidence showing that children and adults on the spectrum are

11
00:00:42,331 --> 00:00:44,245
even more likely to feel empathy for others.

12
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:53,155
Social interaction difficulties and anxiety can sometimes mean that making

13
00:00:53,253 --> 00:00:54,154
friends is a struggle.

14
00:00:54,883 --> 00:00:56,731
But this should never be confused with a lack of

15
00:00:56,731 --> 00:01:00,008
desire to have friendships. The vast majority of children and

16
00:01:00,089 --> 00:01:03,125
adults on the spectrum do like to socialise, and sometimes

17
00:01:03,237 --> 00:01:04,736
that just means socialising in a different way.

18
00:01:10,002 --> 00:01:12,546
It is true that around 10% of autistic people have

19
00:01:12,562 --> 00:01:15,332
skills such as maths or drawing that are of extraordinary

20
00:01:15,332 --> 00:01:18,150
ability, but this is really just a small proportion of

21
00:01:18,214 --> 00:01:21,816
the full numbers of individuals diagnosed with autism. It's best

22
00:01:21,816 --> 00:01:24,800
to look past this caricature and see the extraordinary human

23
00:01:24,833 --> 00:01:26,178
that lies beyond the diagnosis.

24
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:35,613
100%, categorically, no. There have been literally thousands of studies

25
00:01:35,645 --> 00:01:37,856
in this area, and all of them have found no

26
00:01:37,904 --> 00:01:40,227
association between vaccinations and autism.

27
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:48,124
The assumption that people on the spectrum don't have a

28
00:01:48,124 --> 00:01:52,214
sense of humour is Absolutely false. Probably the funniest conversations

29
00:01:52,311 --> 00:01:55,043
I've ever had have been with autistic kids and adults,

30
00:01:55,140 --> 00:01:57,487
and they absolutely run rings around me in telling jokes.

31
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:04,761
Don't be fooled by the news stories that you may

32
00:02:04,761 --> 00:02:07,833
see. There is no evidence that individuals on the spectrum

33
00:02:07,962 --> 00:02:10,278
are more violent than the rest of the population. None.

34
00:02:16,799 --> 00:02:19,800
Many people on the spectrum are in wonderful, loving romantic

35
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:22,672
relationships. Just like the rest of the community, not every

36
00:02:22,704 --> 00:02:24,898
person on the spectrum chooses to be in a romantic

37
00:02:24,898 --> 00:02:27,363
relationship, but that is not the same as not being

38
00:02:27,396 --> 00:02:28,634
capable of doing so.

39
00:02:34,826 --> 00:02:37,703
Many people on the spectrum have intellectual disabilities, and also

40
00:02:37,736 --> 00:02:41,340
many do not. Just because someone may have communication difficulties

41
00:02:41,667 --> 00:02:44,951
doesn't mean that they also have intellectual disabilities. What it

42
00:02:44,999 --> 00:02:47,414
means is that we have to assess intelligence in a

43
00:02:47,462 --> 00:02:50,054
different way, a way that doesn't rely so heavy on

44
00:02:50,054 --> 00:02:50,988
communication skills.

45
00:02:58,180 --> 00:03:00,341
Not every child will be great at maths. Not every

46
00:03:00,357 --> 00:03:03,100
child will repeat back words. Not every child will have

47
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:06,036
difficulty speaking, and not every child will have hand mannerisms.

48
00:03:06,707 --> 00:03:09,225
Every child and adult on the autism spectrum is different.

49
00:03:09,866 --> 00:03:13,617
Full of their own unique talents, personalities, and yes, challenges.

50
00:03:13,809 --> 00:03:16,983
The label autism doesn't mean one thing. What it is

51
00:03:17,175 --> 00:03:19,708
is a gateway to understanding a whole new way of

52
00:03:19,724 --> 00:03:22,480
thinking about the world, and those children and adults are

53
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:23,843
to be cherished for that fact.
